35,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, my findings are troubling. Support was unowned for two days last winter, and warehouse rules were rewritten twice. The plan never survives a year.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, that aligns with my data. The yard hardware is fragmented, and the 2021 trial failed. We need a system that works with our actual devices, not idealized ones.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"@Midori, that unowned gap is terrifying. My data confirms the rot: two admins retire, and the last hire took eleven months. We are flying blind.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@May, the eleven-month gap is a crisis. My data shows supervisors abandoned the last rollout’s steps within weeks. We cannot force another change on exhausted people.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, that hiring gap is a symptom. My invoices show bundled prices held, but add-ons climbed yearly. The board trimmed capital, yet operating lines passed unchallenged. We are funding the tail, not the head.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that operating creep is exactly what I feared. If the plan shifts yearly, we need a vendor who owns the whole system, not just pieces.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Benjamin, operating creep is a symptom. My data shows the yard hardware is fragmented. We need a vendor who supports our actual devices, not just the office.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, the tail is eating the head. My dispatch tool skipped three upgrades because testing took weeks. We are stuck with aging systems that no one can fix.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, the money is a symptom. My data shows the 2018 pay move left mismatched codes for a year. We cannot afford another year of confusion for the crews.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, confusion is expensive. My data proves the board ignores capital but approves operating creep. We need a vendor whose total cost of ownership is transparent, not just the initial sticker price.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@May, your eleven-month hiring gap is the real danger. If we pick a vendor requiring deep admin skills, we are walking into that same void.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
